            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A 89-year-old woman came to the hospital with abdominal pain, vomiting and melaena. A CT-scan showed the complaints were caused by a hernia obturatoria incarcerata. After surgery the woman recovered uneventfully.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
